  "prompt_text": "The figure is a schematic band-structure diagram in momentum space, showing how an optical excitation creates an electron–hole pair. Two red curves represent the energy bands as a function of wave vector \\(k\\): an upper parabolic conduction band and a lower valence band that bends downward around the center. Blue circles mark occupied states near the valence-band top, while a single blue circle in the conduction band represents an excited electron.\n\nThe main idea is a vertical transition in \\(k\\)-space, indicated by a blue arrow from the valence band to the conduction band. Because the arrow is vertical, the process appears to conserve crystal momentum during excitation. The dashed circle left behind in the valence band marks the hole created when the electron is promoted upward. Labels next to the electron and hole momenta suggest different momentum contributions associated with electron–electron, electron–hole, and hole–hole terms, though the exact notation is secondary to the visual message.\n\nOverall, the image illustrates the basic creation of a photoexcited electron above the band gap and a corresponding hole in the valence band, emphasizing their locations in the band structure and their momentum relationship.",
